Model picker: the model name owns the row instead of being cut by prices.

Upstream (v0.23.0) lays a catalog row out on one line: star, name
(`min-w-0 truncate`), then the shrink-0 price, usage and setting chips.
In the 18rem (`w-72`) popover the price column takes most of the width,
so OpenRouter names read "DeepSee…" and "DeepSeek V4.1 Fl…", and dated
variants of one model can't be told apart.

- the name may wrap (`whitespace-normal break-words`), never an ellipsis;
- load bar, price, usage level and setting chips move to a second line
  under the name;
- the row's tooltip (`title`) is the full model id;
- the composer's model popover is wider: min(26rem, 100vw - 2rem).

Test: src/app/shell/model-catalog-menu.full-name.test.tsx (run by
desktop.nix's checkPhase). Upstream's model-catalog-menu.test.tsx found
the name span by `.truncate`, which this patch removes: it now selects
`[data-model-menu-row-name]` (also run by the checkPhase).

